  "summary": "Four studies directly apply federated learning (decentralised training without pooled records) to customer churn (predicting customer attrition), and one applies a multilevel probabilistic model to the same topic. [V0201] (Chen et al., 2019) evaluates on ChurnBench, reporting accuracy 0.78. [V0203] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) evaluates on Atlas-ICU, reporting AUROC 0.92 — the strongest result among the federated approaches. [V0202] (Duarte et al., 2020) evaluates on MetroFlow, reporting MAE 0.85. [V0204] (Fischer et al., 2022) evaluates on AgriSat-4, reporting F1 0.64 — the weakest federated result. [V0211] (Gupta et al., 2023) applies multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling to customer attrition on Atlas-ICU, achieving accuracy 0.79; this is included as the fifth-ranked document because it directly addresses the topic, though it does not use federated learning. Documents such as [V0052] and [V0101] mention federated learning for churn only as prior-work references and are therefore not directly relevant.",
